{"response":{"docs":[{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C4872","ontology_name":"ncit","ontology_prefix":"NCIT","short_form":"NCIT_C4872","description":["A carcinoma arising from the breast, most commonly the terminal ductal-lobular unit. It is the most common malignant tumor in females. Risk factors include country of birth, family history, menstrual and reproductive history, fibrocystic disease and epithelial hyperplasia, exogenous estrogens, contraceptive agents, and ionizing radiation. The vast majority of breast carcinomas are adenocarcinomas (ductal or lobular). Breast carcinoma spreads by direct invasion, by the lymphatic route, and by the blood vessel route. The most common site of lymph node involvement is the axilla."],"label":"Breast Carcinoma","obo_id":"NCIT:C4872","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["Breast Cancer","Breast Carcinoma","Breast cancer, NOS","Cancer of Breast","Cancer of the Breast","Carcinoma of Breast","Carcinoma of the Breast","Mammary Carcinoma","breast cancer"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0004989","ontology_name":"mondo","ontology_prefix":"MONDO","short_form":"MONDO_0004989","broad_synonyms":["breast cancer","breast cancer, NOS","cancer of breast","cancer of the breast","cancer, breast"],"description":["A carcinoma that arises from epithelial cells of the breast"],"label":"breast carcinoma","obo_id":"MONDO:0004989","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["breast carcinoma","carcinoma of breast","carcinoma of the breast","mammary carcinoma"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/DOID_3459","ontology_name":"doid","ontology_prefix":"DOID","short_form":"DOID_3459","description":["A breast cancer that has_material_basis_in abnormally proliferating cells derives_from epithelial cells."],"label":"breast carcinoma","obo_id":"DOID:3459","type":"class","exact_synonyms":["Mammary carcinoma","carcinoma of breast"]},{"iri":"http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/HP_0003002","ontology_name":"hp","ontology_prefix":"HP","short_form":"HP_0003